  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Set at the Nouveau Port in Cavalaire, La Suite serves world cuisine with Italian influences, in an air-conditioned setting extended by a large terrace with harbour views.</p>

      <h2>Practical information</h2>
      <p>According to the PagesJaunes/Mappy listing, the restaurant serves every day from 9am to 2pm and from 7pm to 11pm; the budget given is €21 to €30 per person, with payment by card, holiday vouchers and meal vouchers. The dining room is air-conditioned, the terrace opens onto the harbour and wifi is available. The restaurant also accepts group meals.</p>

      <h2>Check before you go: dog policy</h2>
      <p>Only the PagesJaunes/Mappy directory says "pets accepted". The Cavalaire-sur-Mer tourist office (2025-2026 brochure, which lists La Suite among the bars and restaurants) and the restaurant publish no rule on dogs: so it is not known whether dogs are welcome indoors or on the terrace, or whether there is a size condition. The hours and budget also come from the directory, with no website of the restaurant's own found. Not to be confused with "Le Bateau Ivre", another restaurant at the Nouveau Port that officially confirms it accepts animals.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: call before coming with your dog, or try Le Bateau Ivre instead, a little further along the same harbour.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cavalaire harbour and its promenade are right nearby, perfect for a digestive walk with your dog before or after the meal.</p>
      <p>If you prefer an address whose dog policy is officially published, Le Bateau Ivre (42 Nouveau Port) appears on the Cavalaire tourist office listing with "Animals accepted" (updated 11/05/2026); it is open all year 2026, every day, and its presentation text describes a brasserie-bar with a 180° terrace. For La Suite, however, no official listing consulted gives the precise address on the harbour, the hours or the rule for dogs.</p>
    </div>

